WEBVTT

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.900
Why aren't you angry with me?

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.070
There's no reason to be angry.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.970
So you've finally decided to open your mouth and ask.

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.920
It wasn't easy wondering how long I had to wait for that.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.180
Don't you have any alcohol?

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:46.940
I don't really drink.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.570
If beer's fine with you, I can...

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.980
Go buy some.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:59.510
nemuri nasai ima wa tada

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:59.510
Sleep, for now

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:06.420
watashi no naka de doko ni mo ikanai de

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:06.420
Inside of me, and don't go anywhere

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:27.430
madoromi no fuchi de yureteru gunjou iro no yo

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:27.430
Through the slumbering ultramarine sky

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:32.950
majiwaru koto no nai hoshi wo sagashiteru

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:32.950
I am searching for stars that will never cross

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:40.650
anata wo motomeru yubisaki yami ni samayotte

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:40.650
These fingertips search for you, but are lost in darkness

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:49.530
mogaite mo nukedesenai ai no umi ni oboreteku

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:49.530
I try but I can't escape, and I drown in the sea of love

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:57.420
yawaranai toiki ni kokoro sae mo furueru

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:57.420
Your tender sigh makes my heart tremble

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:03.040
karamaru utsukushi kumo no ito no you

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:03.040
Seemingly entangled in the beautiful strands of a spider web

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:07.530
ugokenai no watashi wo yurushite

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:07.530
I cannot move, please forgive me

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:10.860
anata no ude ni dakarete nemuru

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:10.860
I am sleeping with your arms around me

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.080
nani mo kamo sutetatte ii

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:14.080
I don't mind losing anything else

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:21.610
ii kono mama no maboroshi nante zukuru no wa yamete

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:21.610
Stop pretending that you are a good girl

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:25.070
hontou no watashi wo mitsukete

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:25.070
Find the real me

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:31.150
zutto matteru

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:31.150
I'll be waiting forever

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.130
I showered first.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:51.000
I'm borrowing this.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.090
Please change your clothes right now.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:08.100
Page 20
Love is not rational.
The lovers who said this,
were poets, commentators,
and philosophers.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.800
Didn't I tell you already?!

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.570
I've been cooped up and haven't showered in days.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:15.370
And you're someone who'd care about that?

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.570
The President's waiting for you at the studio.

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:19.830
I can have just one beer, can't I?

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.070
Since Touya-kun went out of his way to-

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.450
You can drink it in the car.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:25.230
Wait, let go of me...

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.680
Let go!

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:36.210
See ya.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:41.300
Touya-kun?

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:50.510
But yesterday, I... did something like that, so I can't go to the festival anymore...

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:53.470
If just this much pressure is enough to enervate you,

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:56.130
then the festival might be too much for you to handle.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.720
Let's have a toast!

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.300
For avoiding a huge waste of time.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.910
Futhermore, isn't this also the first time you opposed me, Yuki?

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:07.470
That's an improvement, and I truly want to be glad about it.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:09.970
In fact, I'm so happy I could reward you.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.540
Why... me?

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.610
That's a silly question.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.430
What's wrong with Rina-chan?

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.440
That's an even sillier question.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:23.950
Rina is my alter-ego.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.180
In other words, she's myself.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.680
And you, Yuki, are everything else.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:30.100
I don't understand!

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.170
Come with me, Yuki.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:35.350
I'll show you your friends.

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:41.070
Be sure to keep this a secret.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.930
Ever since that day, that fateful moment...

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:03.140
...acquiring paintings has become my purpose in life.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.580
I asked Nagase to help me collect them.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.530
I've put a lot of effort, time, and money into this.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:16.770
That's right. As you can see, they're all the same painting.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:20.140
And not a single one of them is the real thing.

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:22.760
All of them are counterfeit.

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.780
FAKE

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:26.150
None of these paintings is the one I saw in London.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.920
That one single painting,

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.810
that I'm looking for,

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.620
even at this very moment...

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:37.780
Rina cannot become the real thing.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:40.350
And, now, neither can you, Yuki.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.710
Ogata-san?

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:50.570
All of these paintings are different...

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.380
Yuki-san!

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:56.460
Oh?

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.440
So you have an eye for paintings, Yuki...

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:01.170
Or do you simply have a problem with your eyesight?

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:05.380
It's true that these paintings aren't exactly identical.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.000
As they were painted by men-

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.960
No, that's not what I meant.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:13.990
I don't really know much about paintings,

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:18.100
but the girls in the paintings are all different.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:21.660
What are you talking about, Yuki?

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.020
What on Earth is wrong with you?

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:26.240
You too, Ogata-san... what's wrong with you?

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:29.770
Are you making fun of me?

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:32.850
Come on, Frankie, say something!

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.160
Hey, you're her manager, aren't you?

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:39.680
How could you allow your artist to make such terrible jokes?

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:16.230
This...

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.760
What is this?

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:21.010
What's the meaning of this?

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:24.670
What's the meaning of this...

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:26.900
What's the meaning of this?!

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:28.760
So you knew?

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:29.650
You knew?

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:30.530
You knew all along?!

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:32.680
Why didn't you tell me?

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:36.710
Why, Frankie?

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:40.060
You knew, and yet you got me all these other paintings?

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:43.450
I understand.

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:46.670
I'm fine now.

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:50.570
Get out.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:51.760
You too, Yuki.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:54.570
Why?

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:57.760
I'm sorry.

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.740
I shouldn't have said anything, right?

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:02.920
I don't know.

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:06.040
But...

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:12.190
Yuki-san, the king might be naked, you know.

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:23.660
What do you think you're doing?

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:26.120
This isn't a damn game!

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.150
Looks like you still can't handle her yet.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:38.170
Sometimes I find myself wishing Rina was just a doll sitting at home.

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:40.140
Better yet, what if she was a painting?

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:45.040
I had no idea you were into paintings, Ei-chan.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.620
Where did you hear that from?

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:52.120
I have a painting I'd like you to see.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:55.110
I wouldn't be of any help. I'm not a connoisseur.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:58.290
It's a painting of a girl, and, let's see...

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:01.500
I think they're lilies. Fairly large ones, too.

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.100
This is it. No question about it.

00:09:06.100 --> 00:09:08.400
You know it? It's by Geoffrey.

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:11.470
I don't know the artist.

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:12.770
Oh, no.

00:09:12.770 --> 00:09:16.530
About a year later, I went back and the painting was gone.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:18.970
But I remember it.

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:20.490
There's no way I'd forget.

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:22.310
This is the painting!

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:24.190
So, you want it?

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.190
You'll let me have it?

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:27.870
Not for free.

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:29.050
Of course.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.150
Tell me how much you want.

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:35.150
You know, how about we play a game?

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:14.460
At that very moment, was my fate already sealed?

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:41.700
What did you come back for?

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:46.370
So, you want to join my friends?

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:49.750
What do you see... right now?

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:54.900
An art exhibition with young girls as the motif.

00:10:58.180 --> 00:11:01.400
Come on. Come over here and take your clothes off.

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.270
I'll examine you.

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:06.330
Let's see if you can stand my appreciation.

00:11:06.330 --> 00:11:10.190
What's the matter? Don't you work for me?

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:11.070
Yes.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:15.800
You'd get down on all fours and lick my shoes if I ordered you to, is that right?

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:16.330
Yes.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.420
Then hurry up and get naked.

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:23.870
Grovel like a dog in front of me and lick my shoes.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:26.580
If you'll really listen to everything I say...

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:30.580
I know. I'll write you a song.

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:31.250
Well?

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:33.690
You're not satisfied?

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:37.180
I see, so you came here to laugh at me?

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:38.700
Strange, isn't it?

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:43.720
The fact that I place such high expectations on this one girl despite not knowing when and how she might fall.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.530
So you're saying it's all Yuki's fault?

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:48.350
Yes, it's all her fault.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:48.920
Why?

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:53.030
Since I found her, everything has changed.

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:55.340
Nothing seemed to fit the rhythm anymore-

00:11:55.590 --> 00:12:00.690
Doesn't that prove just how important Yuki-san's existence is to you?

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.800
Even so, nothing will come out of this...

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:03.980
Good.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:04.890
Eh?

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:09.120
The pressure from Yuki-san has affected you to that extent.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:11.520
So you did come here to laugh at me.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:14.680
I don't blame you that all the paintings look the same to you.

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:18.130
Nor do I blame you for feeling that all of them are fakes.

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:22.250
You never heeded Nagase-san's countless warnings.

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:24.570
All you did was buy every painting you could lay your hands on.

00:12:25.620 --> 00:12:33.190
That's because you don't really remember the one real painting you said you saw in London.

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:35.770
You knew it, but you didn't want to admit it.

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:41.070
You can't forgive yourself for no longer
remembering this one painting you believed in.

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.650
You can't.

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:47.990
You also went as far as to sell Rina-san in order to acquire what you thought would be the real thing.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:49.870
But you knew it wasn't.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:51.620
You just turned a blind eye.

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:53.920
It's fortunate that this happened.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:56.390
How does it feel to have your eyes opened?

00:12:56.400 --> 00:12:59.810
I don't think the price of selling Rina-san was low at all.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:02.180
I don't need you to write me a song.

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:03.930
I'm not a singer.

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:08.200
I was just kidding, idiot.

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:12.330
Frankie, come here.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:14.610
I need to talk to you.

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:18.220
I need you to get rid of those goddamn paintings right now.

00:13:18.220 --> 00:13:21.040
I'm spending the night here, I have things to do.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.550
Hmm, Yuki?

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:24.930
Yes?

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:27.470
Eating sweet things late at night isn't good for you.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:31.310
Right!

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:34.870
Uh, sorry about this afternoon.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:39.890
You went to see my father, didn't you? He told me about it.

00:13:39.890 --> 00:13:42.410
Today was my first day of work with Rina-chan...

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:47.560
I was really nervous, but Rina-chan was her usual self.

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:49.070
She was so dignified and majestic...

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:52.880
What is your relationship with Menou?

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:54.500
We only met once,

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:57.520
at Yuki-, Morikawa Yuki's concert.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:59.410
What were you doing there?

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:03.170
Ah, I see. You used to be Morikawa Yuki's assistant?

00:14:03.430 --> 00:14:06.090
No, not really.

00:14:06.090 --> 00:14:07.820
They're lovers.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.350
What?

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:11.240
He's her boyfriend.

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:15.590
You think it was a bad idea to tell her?

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:18.290
Why? It's not something you needed to hide.

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:22.350
I... guess you're right.

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:24.220
If they start having suspicions, then-

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:25.800
That's not it.

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.530
That's not why I... told her.

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:30.430
Anyway, whatever.

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:31.580
Huh?

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:33.060
What's today's schedule?

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:35.310
Ah, uh...

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:38.110
You should be able to recite each event without looking...

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.270
You mean nothing's planned?

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:42.690
Yes.

00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:44.740
All right.

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:47.860
Well then, we have a seat reserved for Mr. Touya Fujii...

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:49.110
Huh?

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:52.200
...at the Ogata Rina solo live concert. Shall we go?

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:20.350
Liar

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:31.670
Ogata Rina's practice session

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:31.670
lasted five and a half hours

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:38.120
Touya.

00:15:38.280 --> 00:15:38.960
Huh?

00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:41.320
What're you doing here?

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:44.170
What am I doing here? How rude of you.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.960
I have an errand to run with Student Affairs.

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:49.060
Misaki-san and Akira-kun were here a while ago.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:50.310
Really?

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:51.430
Touya...

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:54.650
I wanted to say I'm not coming,

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:57.820
but if everyone's here we could all grab a bite together, since it's been a while.

00:15:57.820 --> 00:15:59.100
I'm not coming.

00:15:59.450 --> 00:16:01.610
I have to go somewhere right now.

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:02.940
With Mana-chan?

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:04.020
By myself.

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:05.030
Bye.

00:16:05.030 --> 00:16:05.820
Hey...

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:08.990
Patch things up with Mana-chan, okay?

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:10.440
We never fought.

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:13.120
Then... nevermind.

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:14.820
It's almost time for her entrance exams, isn't it?

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.530
I don't think it's a good idea to disturb her at this time.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:21.260
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:30.840
We're closed for today - Yuunagi University Student Affairs Office

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:30.840
Excuse me...

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:34.660
You're Fujii-san... right?

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.220
Yeah, umm...

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:38.820
I'm Yamamoto, from Student Affairs.

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:42.800
Ah, thanks for your help back then.

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:44.820
Oh, don't mention it.

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:48.410
So, how was it? The job...

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:50.280
Man, it was tough.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:54.550
I see. I'll find you something else, then.

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:56.960
Oh no, I don't need any more jobs.

00:16:56.960 --> 00:16:57.240
Oh?

00:16:57.600 --> 00:17:00.210
Don't worry about me, I'll continue working.

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:01.420
For now, anyway.

00:17:01.420 --> 00:17:02.990
I see...

00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:05.970
You really did introduce me to a great job, though.

00:17:05.970 --> 00:17:07.180
I need to thank you, too.

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:08.030
Huh?

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:10.340
You called me a savior-goddess.

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:14.800
It was very encouraging and it made me very happy.

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:19.010
I don't really know what to do now at this point. I don't have anything nice-

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:22.180
Umm, I just said it carelessly...

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:24.130
Ah, don't worry about it.

00:17:24.130 --> 00:17:26.220
I just wanted to thank you for it.

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:27.000
Bye.

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:29.420
Umm, Yamamoto-san.

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:30.160
Yes?

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:32.900
Dinner together?

00:17:33.220 --> 00:17:34.480
Kidding, I'm just kidding!

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:36.570
You wouldn't want to have dinner with an old lady like me-

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:37.650
Sure.

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:40.080
Really?

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:41.370
It's just that...

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:45.540
I started a job with irregular working hours yesterday...

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:49.020
I'm fine anytime, since I'm free all the time.

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:50.470
Well then...

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:52.880
Ah, I'm free today.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.420
Today? You mean, after this?

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:58.280
I guess that was a little sudden. In that case...

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:00.510
No, it's fine!

00:18:00.750 --> 00:18:02.930
I'm free. Let's go, right after this.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.930
Well then, please.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:06.020
Yay!

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.210
What would you like to eat?

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:09.940
I know a great French restaurant.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:11.400
I'm fine with anything, anywhere.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.250
Ah, I know.

00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:16.820
As thanks for accompanying me, I'll tell you something good.

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:19.760
You know Mizuki-san? Her family situation...

00:18:23.220 --> 00:18:24.770
That bastard, he's up to it again-

00:18:24.770 --> 00:18:26.300
Let it slide.

00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:30.970
But isn't she an employee from the Student Affairs Office?

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:32.040
He'll sleep with anyone?

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:35.330
Don't say that, they're just having tea.

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:38.160
You know, I knew he was like that ever since I met him-

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:40.090
It's okay, let's go.

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:45.140
What if he was with Haruka instead?

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:47.010
Then it's perfectly fine.

00:18:47.010 --> 00:18:49.870
What about Rina-san... was it? Yuki-san's senior...

00:18:49.870 --> 00:18:51.160
That's impossible.

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:53.770
There's no way Ogata Rina would have tea with Touya.

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:56.650
What if he was with me?

00:18:57.410 --> 00:18:59.400
Then it's the end of our relationship.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:00.110
With who?

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:00.820
With you.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:05.570
That's not good. It's not like you to get jealous.

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:08.380
You mean, like Tamaru?

00:19:10.990 --> 00:19:13.380
What do you know about Tamaru-kun?

00:19:14.660 --> 00:19:17.310
The reason he's like this is because of me.

00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:18.400
Misaki-san?

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:21.840
He's not a bad person. Really.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:22.470
But...

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:25.870
All you did was dump him, right?

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:28.000
Yes, all I did was dump him.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.310
I dumped... him.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:45.640
What's wrong? You don't look very happy all of a sudden.

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:46.990
No, it's nothing.

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:48.160
Are you surprised?

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:52.010
That Mizuki-san's mother is actually
the president of an artist production company...

00:19:55.350 --> 00:19:57.750
I actually am

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:57.750
kind of shocked

00:19:57.350 --> 00:19:59.880
But, why would she actually change her surname?

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.180
Maybe she just didn't want people to know?

00:20:02.990 --> 00:20:05.640
You know, to keep her business and her daughter separate.

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:18.270
E-Excuse me, I have to go to the bathroom.

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:23.550
Why are you going back?

00:20:24.830 --> 00:20:27.650
There is a phone call I must make.

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:29.140
You too, Fujii-san.

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:32.080
We'd just about finished eating, anyway.

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:34.500
Was she your new plaything for today?

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:37.780
She's from the Student Affairs office at my university.

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:40.180
It doesn't look like you need me anymore.

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:41.740
Are you jealous?

00:20:41.740 --> 00:20:43.510
I have no idea what you are talking about.

00:20:43.510 --> 00:20:44.710
So, you <i>are</i> jealous.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:48.080
Please, stop seeing other women.

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:49.100
As I thought.

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:51.200
You won't be able to cope.

00:20:51.190 --> 00:20:53.270
You already have two obstacles to handle.

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:56.480
I'm never going on a date again.

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:05.200
Today, Morikawa Yuki graduates from the song studio Pop Star.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:19.380
So... Yuki had the day off today?

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:24.110
I have no obligation to give the schedules of our artists to a staff member of a competing studio.

00:21:24.110 --> 00:21:25.480
Excuse me for asking.

00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:04.350
Shinozuka-san

00:22:35.050 --> 00:22:39.970
It hurts

00:22:49.460 --> 00:22:56.000
watashi ni itsumo anata wa yasashii

00:22:49.460 --> 00:22:56.000
You have always been kind to me

00:22:56.930 --> 00:23:02.570
sono yasashisa ga fuan ni suru

00:22:56.930 --> 00:23:02.570
But this kindness makes me insecure

00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:11.410
unmei no ito hodokenai you ni

00:23:04.740 --> 00:23:11.410
This string of fate, I'll retie it over and over

00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:18.020
nando mo musubi naoshite

00:23:12.480 --> 00:23:18.020
So that it will never come loose

00:23:19.220 --> 00:23:26.390
tsugi ni au yakusoku dekinai mama

00:23:19.220 --> 00:23:26.390
I don't want to hear you say goodbye

00:23:27.690 --> 00:23:36.340
wakare no kotoba mada kikitaku wa nai yo

00:23:27.690 --> 00:23:36.340
Until we make promises to meet again

00:23:36.670 --> 00:23:44.080
aenai yoru ni yume de aetara

00:23:36.670 --> 00:23:44.080
Even if we can't meet tonight, 
if I can see you in my dreams

00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:51.990
ashita ga tsurakute mo waratte irareru

00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:51.990
Even if tomorrow is difficult I'll be able to smile

00:23:51.990 --> 00:23:59.460
donna ni tooku hanarete ite mo

00:23:51.990 --> 00:23:59.460
No matter how far apart we may become

00:23:59.730 --> 00:24:09.440
tsunagatte ireru to shinjite iru

00:23:59.730 --> 00:24:09.440
I believe that we will still be connected together

00:24:21.420 --> 00:24:23.880
Page 21

00:24:23.880 --> 00:24:26.650
I think I want to return to where the path forks.

00:24:26.650 --> 00:24:28.530
I should have gone right, instead.

00:24:28.530 --> 00:24:32.470
This entire journey has been filled with nothing but regret.

00:24:32.470 --> 00:24:34.050
White Album.
